{
"from": 262,
"to": 264,
"text": "The gates are the standing lint and unit entries; one unit filter and one integration filter that select what this chunk adds; a preservation guard; the harness smoke with G2 and G4 over its home; the native `pre-push`; and the operator's hygiene, push and CI read (`leg = \"operator\"`, the `ci.py conclusion` call, `inputs#I1`)."
},
{
"from": 266,
"to": 269,
"text": "No mutation entry, no witness run and no workflow dispatch is listed (`inputs#I1`). No entry is a live leg: step 12 is held, makes its own record in `evidence/live-revive.md` when it runs, and no entry reads that record. The two one-shot controls of step 11 are implement's, in `evidence/red-green.md`, and are never entries; the two filter entries guard the same cases on every re-run."
},
{
"from": 271,
"to": 274,
"text": "The smoke boots an ordinary `viola run` session: it reads the changed start path and the first snapshot's new field. The harness has no revive verb and gains none; revive itself is proven by the two new root test files. The preservation guard names the base commit, because the operator pass's pre-CI commit moves HEAD onto the chunk."
}
],
